1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,100
That cassette could catch more than music.

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:04,380
It could catch a computer program.

3
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:06,420
In 1980s Brazil,

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,280
a radio show called Clip Informática

5
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:11,260
sent software as sound.

6
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:12,820
With the right equipment,

7
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:15,580
a listener could record the broadcast on tape.

8
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,480
A compatible computer could then try to read

9
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:19,960
those sound patterns as data.

10
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:23,080
Years later, a developer tried to decode

11
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:24,740
an old recording from the show.

12
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,560
What did he find in the noise?

13
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,120
The full story is in the linked video.
